(d/'README.md').write_text("# One bounded fact-origin insertion probe\n\nReuse exact cost-probe-v2 timing/sparse checkpoint apparatus on unchanged full47 scan-projector86d5 source and installed333165B015d CLI. Added observations replace only nine existing own/hot/stat Set.add calls with wrappers preserving original key evaluation, actual Set.add order/return and compiler decisions. Aggregate attempts/new first insertions by finite producer labels, retain at most16 first-key samples per set per pass (48 total), reset diagnostic bookkeeping at existing pass entry. Key labels/active definitions are suffix256+length; truncated samples cannot establish unique identity. Underlying compiler sets retain original behavior and are not replaced or bounded.\n\nProducer sites distinguish borrowed-origin consumption/callee-slot ownership, arm disagreement, unresolved borrow finalization, hot family/erased-slot/wildcard/type/constructor, static constructor. First membership is tested before original add; recording follows original mutation. Body/phase/top32 timing remains instrumented elapsed/CPU observed window. Added has/counters/sample allocation/string copies and repeated sparse snapshot serialization introduce additional overhead; no stock timing equivalence/cause/performance claim. Diagnostic pass counters cover only work actually reached, not universal origins.\n\nONE emit30 CPU11 via existing unchanged collector/internal shared lock, same ELF Bun file mode with BUN_BE_BUN=1; no profile/custom cutoff/signal/build/runtime/new dependency/core/source/compiler-algorithm/cap change. Event/pass checkpoint every128 completed definitions preserves flushed partial statistics if timeout; interrupted/unflushed body/origin work remains unknown. Timeout may precede a pass's first128 checkpoint; no inference from absence. Compiler experiment requires independent full launch review before execution. Literal inverse restores exact installed bytes. Old cost and stock30/90 failures remain separate, no retry/acceptance reinterpretation.\n")
